// appending a whole array is one allocation and, for an element type that copies as bytes, one `memcpy`.
//
// This is the kind of thing that regresses without anything failing: an `extend` written as a push loop
// produces the same elements, just one store and two calls at a time, and no OUT section would notice.
// `arr::merge` *was* that loop, which is why it is written through this now.
array<int32> $a = [1, 2, 3];
array<int32> $b = [4, 5];

$a->extend($b);

echo $a->count();
echo $a[3];
echo $a[4];
